<title>UK: Tesco looks at south-east Asia - report.</title>
<headline>Tesco looks at south-east Asia - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tesco Plc, Britain's biggest supermarket group, is considering plans for expansion in south-east Asia, according to Monday's edition of the Financial Times.</p>
<p>The report said Tesco was the first of Britain's supermarket giants to examine entry into the fast growing markets of the region, and had sent a senior manager to Hong Kong to contact possible partners.</p>
<p>Primary targets were likely to be Hong Kong and China, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717.</p>
